edures and legal processes for contesting orders, generating demand for legal representation."}],"plainSummary":"This bill would allow family members and law enforcement to ask federal courts to temporarily prohibit someone from buying or possessing firearms if that person poses a danger to themselves or others. It would make it a federal crime for individuals subject to these orders to have guns, require the FBI to track such orders nationwide, and provide grants to help states and tribes create or enforce similar laws. The bill sets out procedures for issuing, contesting, and renewing these temporary restrictions.","classificationMethod":"llm","plain":{"whoItTouches":"People caught up in the criminal law, and victims of crime.","confidence":"crs-summary"},"topOverlap":{"bioguideId":"C001091","score":0.03343276735938982},"overlapCount":109},"meaning":{"percentile":66.21386826725636,"median":0.010636331736930488,"n":6331,"ordinary":[{"kind":"state-industry","text":"Lawyers & Lobbyists is also the top donor sector for 2 other members from CA. That points to the industry being big in the state, not to anything about this member."}],"unattributedShare":0.4422392180670907}},{"billId":"119-hr-1810","bioguideId":"C001110","cycle":2026,"score":0.003846020346913798,"matches":[{"industry":"education","donorAmount":3620,"donorShare":0.003846020346913798,"billConfidence":0.95,"contribution":0.003846020346913798}],"method":{"formula":"score = Σ_industries ( donorShare(industry) × billWeight(industry) ), where billWeight = classifierConfidence / Σ classifierConfidence. Range 0–1, read as a weighted share of disclosed itemized money.","donorProfileCycle":2026,"billClassificationMethod":"llm","unclassifiedDonorShare":0.4422392180670907},"bill":{"id":"119-hr-1810","congress":119,"billType":"hr","billNumber":"1810","title":"Safe Schools Improvement Act","introducedDate":"2025-03-03","latestActionDate":"2025-03-03","latestActionText":"Referred to the House Committee on Education and 